      //       objdump -h build/CMakeFiles/wb_serve.dir/WebStart.cpp.obj
      //         | grep -c debug_info   ->   0
      //   Zero line table for WebStart.cpp means gdb has nothing to bind a
      //   breakpoint TO. It does not warn; it just runs past. The exe does carry
      //   a few tiny .debug_* sections (~95 KB of .debug_info in a 17 MB binary),
      //   which is why "the exe has debug sections" is a trap -- those come from
      //   a handful of third-party objects, not from our TUs. Always ask the
      //   .obj of the file you want to break in, never the exe.
      //   build_dbg\ by contrast: "CXX_FLAGS = -g -std=c++1z".
      //
      //   WHY NOT ADD -g TO build\. It is the measurement dir. Every recorded
      //   baseline, gate number and byte-comparison in docs/ was taken there,
      //   and this file has carried "keep build\ byte-comparable with every
